sec.p:
For each host i (i = 1,…,N), we can derive the individual reproduction number Ri, which represent the expected numbers of secondary infections caused by an infected host at the start of the epidemic. When Ri >1, infection of the focal farm would cause on average more than one subsequent infection if all other farms in the vicinity were susceptible. When the infectious periods are drawn from a parametric distribution, Ri can be derived explicitly. In our case, the infectious periods T are drawn from a gamma distribution and Ri is given by [5]:




Ri=∑j≠i{1−[11+wh(rij)]c}


(6)
